     "_key": "CXH9EKkg0O5KO4YpbyxlwW",
     "name": "Why I'm standing",
     "value": "I am standing up for human rights and promoting policy for a better economy. The ALCP want law reform for recreational cannabis. 1.4 million people voted YES in the 2020 cannabis referendum they should not  be criminalised, limiting job and travel prospects. Abolishing the expensive, failed Misuse of Drugs Act 1975, will save millions of dollars per annum, better spent on housing, education, school lunches, health and infrastructure. Regulating cannabis will bring jobs, tax revenue."
    },
    {
     "_key": "CXH9EKkg0O5KO4Ypbyxlzi",
     "name": "About me",
     "value": "I am born, educated and along with my husband, worked in our own business in Christchurch. Our second hand curio shop was destroyed in the 2011 earthquake  and currently, in  the accommodation sector of the tourism industry.  I am interested in preservation of heritage, a member of Englefield Residents Neighbourhood group, life member of WILPF Women's International League for Peace and Freedom and member of Macedonian Culture Group my ancestral heritage. Passionate for Human Rights."
    }
